near ruts that mark delineate an old trail.  The stones, many of them cracked,

are overgrown with grass and covered with patches of green-hued velvety moss. 

Westward, the trail gently slopes downward, while to the east, it cuts a

fairly level path, in the direction of the Black Hills Road.

