"stack flat rocks stones grass moss green velvety"
"Insinuating itself into every possible crack in the flat grey stones, long

blades of grass all but hide the stack from view.  Irregularly-shaped patches

of moss turn the rocks into a patchwork pattern of yellow and grey.  The moss

is velvety in texture, an odd contrast to the unyielding surface of the

stone.  There are odd scribings on the topmost stone, spiderwebbed with

thread-like fissures.  The markings, underscored by a dual-tipped arrow,

pointing east and west, reads:


@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@eOrlumber@I@I@I@I@I@eBlack Hills Road@n

@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@I@e<--------------------->@n

"
