caked soil.  It is wide enough to walk in and continues in a slightly

irregular fashion westward.  The slope to the south is gentle enough to allow

precarious passage out of this ravine.  Various prints are frozen into the

dried earth underfoot, evidence that at some time, there was enough water to

turn the ground into mud.

